| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Architecture | Guest OS | Shared Host OS |
| Boot Time | Minutes | Seconds |
| Resource Efficiency | Heavy/High RAM | Lightweight/Low RAM |
| Isolation Level | Hardware-level | Process-level |

**Summary for CloudNova Technologies Client:**
You should consider moving your web applications to containers instead of traditional Virtual Machines because containers utilize a shared host operating system, making them incredibly lightweight. This eliminates the need to boot a full Guest OS, reducing startup times from minutes to mere seconds. Furthermore, containers isolate processes efficiently, ensuring your applications consume significantly less RAM and CPU while remaining highly scalable.
